Z||000000||camon||11-19-2001||11:42 PM||||I was wondering.......<P>I seen some mention here on the board of a manifold recall!<P>If this is accurate I was wonering what the recall focused on (what was the problem)?<P>How can I check to see what recalls have been performed on my 87 GT (including the manifold recall if in fact there was one)!<P>Also if some recalls haven't been completed on my car can they still be done free of charge by a GM dealership?<P>------------------<BR>Keith||||reg||5
Z||000001||Mike Murphy||11-20-2001||12:42 AM||||You can try calling 1-800-762-2737 and talk with a Customer Relationhip Manager.  I tried that last week and they could not tell me if a recall had been done or not.  I assumed they had purged the system after so many years so the next best thing to do is to put it in writing.  In about a week I recieved a letter from the same department asking me to contact them with a reference number to my inquiry they had assinged to it.  After a brief discussing their representative agreed to research any and all outstanding campaigns on my 3 Fieros.<P>They are obligated to repair at no cost to the current owner no matter how many miles are on the vehicle or how many owners it has had or the number of years old the car may be.<P>Having the dealer check may not help as they use the same system.<P>I would put it in writing if they can't help you on the 1st try by phone.<P><BR>Mike Murphy<BR>Former PMD DSM||||reg||12
Z||000002||Nashco||11-20-2001||12:57 AM||||Here's a really good thread to read, it's got tons of info on it, and links to even more.  Read away grasshopper! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20010924-2-010706.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20010924-2-010706.html</A> <P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
